B10 patch for the check-in owner (Oct 19, 2026). Not applied: these three
files are outside B10. Apply from the repo root with `git apply <this file>`
(checked with `git apply --check` against main a3215a1 + the B10 working tree).

1. The student's check-in page names the day, in campus time, like the door.
   Today, a link opened the night before says "Check-in opens at 6:00 PM, an
   hour before the event." while the door says "Check-in opens tomorrow at
   6:00 PM.". After: "Check-in opens tomorrow at 6:00 PM, an hour before the
   event." The day-aware phrase comes from `checkinOpensWhen` in
   src/components/events/checkin/door-screen.ts (pure, no React, B10's file),
   which the door already uses.

   Why not move it into src/lib/events/event-checkin.ts as the review asked:
   it needs campus-time.ts, which imports "@/lib/push/event-notice". At least
   six test files load event-checkin.ts with plain type stripping and no "@/"
   resolve hook (event-checkin, qr-path, use-checkin-state, checkin-migration,
   attendees-route...), so an "@/" import there would break them all. So
   event-checkin.ts keeps only the wording (`opensAtLine(when)`) and stays
   import-free.

2. The shared `doorStartLead` gets the door's new words ("the QR code or the 4
   numbers next to it"; "under the code" was wrong from 760 px wide). DoorView
   now draws its own copy (DOOR_START_LEAD), so after this patch the shared key
   is unused: keep it equal, or delete it. CONTRACT.md line 1324 has the old
   words too.

Checks run on a scratch copy: event-checkin.test.ts passes (its one source
check that reads campus-home.tsx can't run outside the repo). Not run:
tsc/eslint on CheckinLanding.tsx with the patch in.

